  "person_4": "NURSE",
  "person_5": "UNKNOWN"
 },
 "turns": [
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Good morning. The booking says an eczema flare in Ivy. Hello, Ivy! Mum, give me the headlines, I know you're busy. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Thanks. It's a flare. Behind her knees and in her elbows, red and rough, for about a week. I've got to be at the bank by eleven."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "A week. And is she itchy?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Very. She rubs her legs on the carpet."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_5",
   "t": "[from the doorway] She was scratching all night, I heard her!"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Sorry, who was that? I didn't catch it. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "I think that's my sister, she's waiting outside. Ignore her. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Noted, a voice from the doorway says she scratched through the night. Ivy, show me your legs, sweetheart?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Itchy! ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I can see they're itchy. Nurse, can you do her obs while I write? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_4",
   "t": "Of course. Temperature 36.8, pulse 110, breathing 24, oxygen 98 percent, weight 13.1 kilos, and height 88 centimetres.",
   "pause": 15.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Thank you. Mum, any weeping, crusting, fever?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "No, nothing wet, and no fever."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And what are you using on it?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Epaderm ointment, twice a day, all over. Hydrocortisone cream, once a day on the flares. And cetirizine, maybe 2.5 mg at night, I'd have to look at the bottle."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Okay. We'll check the bottle. Any history in Ivy?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Eczema since she was six months old. And she had bronchiolitis at one."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Does she go to nursery?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Three days a week."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And what does she eat?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Mostly home-cooked. I'm a bit boring that way."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Let me see. Ivy, can I look at your knees, like a doctor in a film?",
   "pause": 10.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Ivy, be good for the doctor. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I can see dry, red, scaly patches behind both knees and in the elbow creases, with a few scratch marks."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Is it infected? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any wheeze or cough with it?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "No, nothing, her chest has been fine."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And her tummy, any vomiting or loose stools?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "No, nothing like that, everything's normal."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "This looks like an eczema flare, nothing more."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Phew. So no change in what we use? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Keep the emollient going, and the hydrocortisone only on the red areas, for up to a week. Pat her dry after baths, don't rub."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Okay. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I'd like to see you again in four weeks to make sure it's settled."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Four weeks. I'll book at the desk. Come on, Ivy. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Bye-bye. ~"
  }
